WEBVTT

00:07.195 --> 00:10.197
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:10.198 --> 00:13.599
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:13.600 --> 00:17.169
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:17.170 --> 00:20.172
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:20.173 --> 00:23.676
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:23.677 --> 00:26.812
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:26.813 --> 00:28.380
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:28.381 --> 00:30.182
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:30.183 --> 00:34.547
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:43.068 --> 00:45.231
Ah, the Feast of San Gennaro.

00:45.232 --> 00:47.266
Every child here has seen a relative

00:47.267 --> 00:48.934
murdered in a barber chair.

00:48.935 --> 00:50.591
Step right up!

00:50.592 --> 00:53.567
Teach an old Italian
lady how to use an iPad!

00:53.568 --> 00:55.708
Now, that sounds like
fun. I'll give it a try.

00:55.709 --> 00:58.544
Hey, how are you? Look
what I got for you.

00:58.545 --> 01:00.735
What is it? It's a tablet computer.

01:00.736 --> 01:01.770
I don't want it.

01:01.771 --> 01:03.122
But you don't even know what it is.

01:03.123 --> 01:04.123
I don't want it.

01:04.124 --> 01:05.557
But you can watch movies on it.

01:05.558 --> 01:06.625
My eyes hurt.

01:06.626 --> 01:08.327
I'm trying to do something nice here!

01:08.328 --> 01:09.928
For the last time, I don't want it.

01:09.929 --> 01:12.598
I bet you if Joey was giving
it to you, you'd take it.

01:12.599 --> 01:13.832
Don't you bring him into this.

01:13.833 --> 01:15.234
Joey was a good boy.

01:15.235 --> 01:16.869
Oh, yeah, yeah, Joey was a good boy?

01:16.870 --> 01:19.271
You thought he was making 100
grand a year hauling lumber?

01:19.272 --> 01:20.439
Don't you start with this.

01:20.440 --> 01:21.774
He was dirty, Ma!

01:21.775 --> 01:23.842
I can't hear this! I won't hear it!

01:23.843 --> 01:25.611
- He was an angel!
- Oh, that's right.

01:25.612 --> 01:28.013
"Angel Joey," great
Joey, perfect Joey.

01:28.014 --> 01:29.548
I got to go to the church.

01:29.549 --> 01:30.849
Oh, yeah, sure, light another candle.

01:30.850 --> 01:31.850
That'll bring him back.

01:31.851 --> 01:33.118
You watch your tongue.

01:33.119 --> 01:35.854
Admit it, you wish it was me
in that car instead of him!

01:35.855 --> 01:37.890
Just take your little TV and go!

01:37.891 --> 01:39.558
It's an iPad, you dumb cow!

01:40.827 --> 01:43.829
I guess I don't have any sons now.

01:43.830 --> 01:46.398
Ma! I'm sorry, Ma!

01:46.399 --> 01:48.765
Ma! Ma!

01:49.135 --> 01:50.903
Hey, Bri, look over there.

01:50.904 --> 01:53.005
That guy looks like Frank Sinatra, Jr.

01:53.006 --> 01:54.340
Stewie, this is Federal Hill.

01:54.341 --> 01:56.484
Everybody looks like
Frank Sinatra, Jr.

01:56.485 --> 01:57.076
Well, then who's that guy

01:57.077 --> 01:58.877
who looks like a young Frank Sinatra?

01:58.878 --> 02:00.713
Oh, that's Woody Allen's
son, but you're right,

02:00.714 --> 02:03.048
that other guy behind him
is Frank Sinatra, Jr.

02:03.049 --> 02:04.683
Stewie! Elliot!

02:04.684 --> 02:06.318
It-it's actually Brian.

02:06.319 --> 02:08.187
We've-we've met many times before.

02:08.188 --> 02:09.747
Then who's Elliot?

02:09.748 --> 02:11.299
I-I really wouldn't know.

02:11.300 --> 02:13.258
This is a bad start to
whatever we're doing.

02:13.259 --> 02:15.661
Well, now, what brings you
fellas to the festival?

02:15.662 --> 02:17.830
My dad will drive long
distances for ice

02:17.831 --> 02:19.164
with colored liquid in it.

02:19.165 --> 02:20.299
They got blue!

02:20.300 --> 02:22.067
And we all love the Italian food.

02:22.068 --> 02:23.969
Oh, you like Italian food?

02:23.970 --> 02:25.337
Want a meatball?

02:25.338 --> 02:27.473
Yeah, I'm gonna pass on
that, but it's a shame

02:27.474 --> 02:30.142
we can't get good Italian
food like this in Quahog.

02:30.143 --> 02:32.411
Well, maybe the three
of us ought to open

02:32.412 --> 02:34.079
an Italian restaurant there.

02:34.080 --> 02:36.220
Open our own Italian restaurant?

02:36.221 --> 02:37.916
I say, that sounds fun.

02:37.917 --> 02:40.919
You, uh, you keep
meatballs in your jacket?

02:40.920 --> 02:43.760
Oh, yeah, all my pockets are
lined with Reynolds Wrap.

02:43.761 --> 02:45.395
I learned that from my old buddies:

02:45.396 --> 02:47.731
Dean Martin, Jr., Joey Bishop, Jr.,

02:47.732 --> 02:49.565
and Sammy Davis the Third.

02:50.635 --> 02:52.235
Hey, where's Chris?

02:52.236 --> 02:54.137
He's over there playing
that carnival game.

02:54.138 --> 02:55.438
Step right up!

02:55.439 --> 02:58.408
Everybody take a chance
on Whack-a-Big-a-Pussy!

02:58.409 --> 03:01.645
Hey, Ton'!

03:01.646 --> 03:03.947
This is not what I thought it was!

03:06.350 --> 03:09.010
Oh, my God, Chris is out of control!

03:09.011 --> 03:09.719
I know!

03:09.720 --> 03:12.355
It must be all the violence
in movies and sex on TV.

03:12.356 --> 03:13.557
Oh.

03:13.558 --> 03:15.024
See, I listen.

03:20.364 --> 03:22.232
Peter, we need to talk
about what happened

03:22.233 --> 03:23.300
at the street fair.

03:23.301 --> 03:25.035
Lois, it's an Italian festival.

03:25.036 --> 03:26.503
You're supposed to yell "Bella, Bella"

03:26.504 --> 03:28.538
and grab as much fat ass as you can.

03:28.539 --> 03:30.440
No, I'm talking about Chris.

03:30.441 --> 03:33.343
I had no idea he had so
much pent-up aggression.

03:33.344 --> 03:36.179
We have to deal with his anger
issues before he hurts himself.

03:36.180 --> 03:37.581
Ah, that's good thinking, Lois.

03:37.582 --> 03:38.782
I've seen what happens

03:38.783 --> 03:40.784
when people hold in their
aggression for too long.

03:40.785 --> 03:43.085
Don't forget, I was in
that elevator with Jay-Z.

03:44.255 --> 03:46.056
Hey, could you have
your guy hit "two"?

03:46.057 --> 03:47.924
I got to get down to
the business center

03:47.925 --> 03:49.326
to print out my boarding pass.

03:49.327 --> 03:51.461
Oh! Hey! That's gonna leave a mark!

03:51.462 --> 03:53.229
That's from a movie.

03:53.230 --> 03:55.799
So, you girls traveling
with your dad here?

03:55.800 --> 03:57.267
Hey, don't kick him, Muddy Shoes.

03:57.268 --> 03:58.902
He's got a white suit on.

03:58.903 --> 04:01.438
Hey, look, I don't know if you
guys are really staying here,

04:01.439 --> 04:04.073
but you can't get into the
pool without a room key.

04:07.712 --> 04:10.080
Okay, Chris, your mom
and I want to help you

04:10.081 --> 04:12.549
get out some of that aggression,
so I thought you and me

04:12.550 --> 04:14.450
could huck rotten
apples at passing cars.

04:16.520 --> 04:19.589
Oh, I didn't know we had
brown apple in the forecast.

04:19.590 --> 04:21.390
Welp, we needed it.

04:23.995 --> 04:26.295
Wow, can I have a turn?

04:33.104 --> 04:35.972
Hey, which one of you threw
that apple at my car?

04:35.973 --> 04:37.741
He did it. He dragged me out here.

04:37.742 --> 04:39.275
I wanted to be in school, sir.

04:39.276 --> 04:41.311
Where'd you get a
cannon like that, kid?

04:41.312 --> 04:43.613
I work out my right arm
three times a day.

04:43.614 --> 04:44.748
Mm, Free weights?

04:44.749 --> 04:47.550
No, mostly JPEGs of Helen
Hunt on my hard drive.

04:47.551 --> 04:49.719
Well, I'm Coach Doyle, and I
head up the baseball team

04:49.720 --> 04:50.787
at James Woods High.

04:50.788 --> 04:53.156
What fake class do they
also make you teach?

04:53.157 --> 04:55.191
- Driver's ed, right?
- No, wood shop.

04:55.192 --> 04:56.760
Ah, that was my second guess.

04:56.761 --> 04:58.595
Tell me, son, how would
you like to pitch

04:58.596 --> 04:59.896
for the high school team?

04:59.897 --> 05:02.265
Baseball's the sport people
play while eating, right?

05:02.266 --> 05:04.768
Oh, yeah, sometimes I even
watch a whole Blacklist.

05:04.769 --> 05:06.970
I don't know, I've never
played baseball before.

05:06.971 --> 05:09.039
Oh, come on, Chris, you got to do it.

05:09.040 --> 05:10.440
If you don't, you'll regret it.

05:10.441 --> 05:13.710
Just like Jesus' friend, Evan,
who bailed on the Last Supper.

05:13.711 --> 05:15.979
Aw, they did a painting?

05:15.980 --> 05:18.631
I would've gone if I knew they
were gonna do a painting.

05:22.887 --> 05:24.320
Here we are, fellas.

05:24.321 --> 05:27.724
The future site of Quahog's
newest Italian restaurant.

05:27.725 --> 05:29.626
Wow, this is a great location.

05:29.627 --> 05:30.927
Can we afford this?

05:30.928 --> 05:32.095
Sure we can.

05:32.096 --> 05:33.797
I set up one of those Kickstarters.

05:33.798 --> 05:35.498
Then I realized how stupid that is

05:35.499 --> 05:38.068
and I went to the bank for
a loan like an adult.

05:38.069 --> 05:40.770
Now, fellas, the tables should
all be bolted to the floor

05:40.771 --> 05:42.172
to prevent theft.

05:42.173 --> 05:43.907
You know, most restaurants
go out of business

05:43.908 --> 05:46.109
because people are
stealing the tables.

05:46.110 --> 05:48.678
The toilets should also
be bolted to the floor.

05:48.679 --> 05:50.780
I think that's pretty
standard, Frank, but okay.

05:50.781 --> 05:52.849
Great. Now let's go find
some chump's restaurant

05:52.850 --> 05:55.050
and steal his tables and toilets.

06:03.728 --> 06:06.496
James Woods is winning for
now, but y'all never know

06:06.497 --> 06:08.732
what might happen in
the moments to come.

06:08.733 --> 06:10.900
I mean, look, there's
two baseball guys

06:10.901 --> 06:12.602
out on the bases right now.

06:12.603 --> 06:15.070
What if they's run to
the scoring place?

06:18.609 --> 06:20.944
Oh, here comes a new boy.

06:20.945 --> 06:22.545
All right, Chris!

06:22.546 --> 06:24.814
Wow, I've never seen him
run onto a baseball field

06:24.815 --> 06:27.751
when he wasn't chasing a duck
or being chased by a duck.

06:27.752 --> 06:29.119
That a duck over there?

06:29.120 --> 06:30.120
Ah, come on!

06:30.121 --> 06:31.654
What the hell's Coach Doyle thinking

06:31.655 --> 06:33.457
bringing in that fat slob?!

06:33.458 --> 06:34.416
You know what?

06:34.417 --> 06:38.428
I bet you a hundred bucks that
"fat slob" strikes this kid out.

06:38.429 --> 06:40.229
Ha, you're on.

06:43.267 --> 06:44.501
Strike one!

06:48.272 --> 06:49.640
Strike two!

06:49.641 --> 06:50.791
Ooh!

06:58.682 --> 07:00.016
Strike three!

07:02.052 --> 07:04.354
Three strikes and he's out,

07:04.355 --> 07:06.955
just like my cousin
Freddie with the drugs.

07:08.025 --> 07:10.560
Holy crap, a hundred bucks!

07:10.561 --> 07:11.860
Hey, nice going, Chris!

07:13.664 --> 07:16.099
Wow, look how proud my dad is.

07:16.100 --> 07:17.733
Oh, my God, a duck!

07:19.136 --> 07:20.503
It was a trap!

07:27.782 --> 07:30.317
Guys, tonight the drinks are on me.

07:30.318 --> 07:33.086
I just won a hundred bucks
off Chris's baseball game.

07:33.087 --> 07:34.788
Really? How'd you do that?

07:34.789 --> 07:37.457
This dad took one look at
Chris and thought he'd suck,

07:37.458 --> 07:39.593
but it turns out Chris
is a great pitcher.

07:39.594 --> 07:42.362
I'm so proud of the money
I won betting on him.

07:42.363 --> 07:44.865
You know, I bet there are
plenty of other baseball dads

07:44.866 --> 07:46.467
who'd also assume Chris stinks.

07:46.468 --> 07:47.801
Peter, we could make a lot of money.

07:47.802 --> 07:50.604
Yeah, we could make
Toni Braxton money.

07:50.605 --> 07:52.406
Is that... is that a lot?

07:52.407 --> 07:54.742
It's a lot, and then nothing.

07:54.743 --> 07:58.130
And then a record whose proceeds
go directly to creditors.

08:05.988 --> 08:08.122
♪ Put me in, Coach ♪

08:08.123 --> 08:10.692
♪ I'm ready to play ♪

08:10.693 --> 08:12.093
♪ Today ♪

08:12.094 --> 08:14.729
♪ Put me in, Coach ♪

08:14.730 --> 08:17.465
♪ I'm ready to play ♪

08:17.466 --> 08:18.866
♪ Today ♪

08:18.867 --> 08:20.968
♪ Look at me ♪

08:20.969 --> 08:22.303
♪ I can be ♪

08:22.304 --> 08:23.637
♪ Centerfield ♪

08:26.175 --> 08:29.477
♪ Well, I spent some time
in the Mudville Nine ♪

08:29.478 --> 08:32.213
♪ Watching it from the bench ♪

08:32.214 --> 08:34.082
♪ You know I took some lumps ♪

08:34.083 --> 08:36.516
♪ When the Mighty Casey struck out ♪

08:39.021 --> 08:41.355
♪ So Say Hey Willie ♪

08:41.356 --> 08:42.857
♪ Tell the Cobb ♪

08:42.858 --> 08:45.693
♪ And Joe DiMaggio ♪

08:45.694 --> 08:47.729
♪ Don't say it ain't so ♪

08:47.730 --> 08:51.064
♪ You know the time is now. ♪

08:58.160 --> 08:59.540
Frank, where the hell is everybody?

08:59.541 --> 09:01.409
This was supposed to be
our big opening night.

09:01.410 --> 09:03.144
I'll tell you what the problem is.

09:03.145 --> 09:06.146
Every successful restaurant
has a hook or a gimmick.

09:06.147 --> 09:07.348
That's what we're lacking.

09:07.349 --> 09:09.183
No, we're not.

09:09.184 --> 09:11.554
Frank, you're the hook! That's right.

09:11.555 --> 09:13.875
We just need to make you the
face of the restaurant.

09:13.876 --> 09:16.204
It may be the five
loaves of garlic bread

09:16.205 --> 09:19.674
I ate this morning talking, but
I think that's a swell idea.

09:26.749 --> 09:28.483
♪ You'll love the meal ♪

09:28.484 --> 09:30.118
♪ The fancy feel ♪

09:30.119 --> 09:33.388
♪ The showbiz stories
while you eat your veal ♪

09:33.389 --> 09:36.558
♪ It's family dining
with a mobster feel ♪

09:36.559 --> 09:39.127
♪ At Frank Sinatra's restaurant ♪

09:39.128 --> 09:40.128
Junior!

09:40.129 --> 09:41.763
♪ The wine is red ♪

09:41.764 --> 09:43.465
♪ With lots of bread ♪

09:43.466 --> 09:46.968
And portions bigger
than a horse's head.

09:46.969 --> 09:50.238
♪ You'll burp up sausages
tonight in bed ♪

09:50.239 --> 09:54.042
♪ At Frank Sinatra's restaurant ♪

09:54.043 --> 09:55.643
♪ Here's a toast ♪

09:57.246 --> 09:59.313
♪ To our host ♪

10:00.683 --> 10:03.985
♪ The food's not great, but ♪

10:03.986 --> 10:06.755
♪ Drink enough and you won't know ♪

10:06.756 --> 10:10.125
♪ The guests will swoon
and Frank will croon ♪

10:10.126 --> 10:13.161
♪ A "beep-bop-dooby-dop"
Italian tune ♪

10:13.162 --> 10:15.230
♪ You dine like royalty ♪

10:15.231 --> 10:18.766
♪ At Frank Sinatra's restaurant ♪

10:21.838 --> 10:25.407
♪ We got big plans
to please our fans ♪

10:25.408 --> 10:28.844
♪ Our cocktail waitress
has enormous cans ♪

10:28.845 --> 10:31.446
♪ A men's room servant who
will dry your hands ♪

10:31.447 --> 10:34.883
♪ At Frank Sinatra's restaurant ♪

10:34.884 --> 10:38.553
♪ Our pizza pies could win a prize ♪

10:38.554 --> 10:41.623
♪ The jukebox catalog is double size ♪

10:41.624 --> 10:44.392
♪ It plays both Capitol
and, yes, Reprise ♪

10:44.393 --> 10:45.594
That's "Repreeze."

10:45.595 --> 10:48.096
♪ At Frank Sinatra's restaurant ♪

10:48.097 --> 10:51.198
♪ Gorgeous views ♪

10:52.268 --> 10:55.137
♪ And top-shelf booze ♪

10:55.138 --> 10:57.739
♪ Yes, we serve Jews ♪

10:57.740 --> 11:01.476
♪ Um, that was never an issue ♪

11:01.477 --> 11:03.311
♪ So, raise your glass ♪

11:03.312 --> 11:05.080
♪ You'll have a gas ♪

11:05.081 --> 11:08.116
♪ But seating's limited,
so move your ass ♪

11:08.117 --> 11:09.951
♪ And plant it firmly ♪

11:09.952 --> 11:14.789
♪ Here at Frank Sinatra's restaurant ♪

11:14.790 --> 11:17.792
♪ Frank's restaurant ♪

11:17.793 --> 11:24.132
♪ Frank's res... taurant. ♪

11:33.142 --> 11:34.743
Wow!

11:34.744 --> 11:36.144
Look at this, guys.

11:36.145 --> 11:39.080
I can't believe we made
all this in one game.

11:39.081 --> 11:40.448
Yeah, I'm having a great time

11:40.449 --> 11:42.517
handling this money and
then touching my eyeball.

11:42.518 --> 11:45.654
Jerome, another round
for my blurry friends.

11:45.655 --> 11:47.189
Yeah, we got a good thing going.

11:47.190 --> 11:49.224
We just have to keep
Chris's talent a secret.

11:49.225 --> 11:51.159
Good evening, I'm Tom Tucker.

11:51.160 --> 11:53.695
Our top story tonight, the
James Woods High baseball team

11:53.696 --> 11:55.797
is headed to the
district championship,

11:55.798 --> 11:59.267
thanks to their secret weapon,
star pitcher Chris Griffin.

11:59.268 --> 12:01.870
Ah, crap, now everyone
knows Chris is a ringer!

12:01.871 --> 12:04.005
Tom Tucker just ruined everything.

12:04.006 --> 12:06.807
This sucks even worse than
when I stubbed my toe.

12:08.277 --> 12:09.611
Aah!

12:09.612 --> 12:12.714
Why does everything bad
always happen to me?!

12:12.715 --> 12:16.384
Answer me, guy in box
and guy on cross!

12:22.925 --> 12:24.526
Stewie, can I talk to you?

12:24.527 --> 12:27.062
Look, Brian, I affectionately
pat all the waiters on the ass.

12:27.063 --> 12:28.930
And if anyone has a problem with it,

12:28.931 --> 12:30.298
they should come to me directly!

12:30.299 --> 12:31.566
No, no, it's not that.

12:31.567 --> 12:32.867
I-I've been going
through our receipts,

12:32.868 --> 12:34.502
and we're actually losing money.

12:34.503 --> 12:36.071
Well, yeah, duh.

12:36.072 --> 12:37.505
Frank comps every meal.

12:37.506 --> 12:38.974
Look, he's doing it again.

12:38.975 --> 12:40.976
Little-known secret
about Charlton Heston.

12:40.977 --> 12:42.744
Never used toilet paper.

12:42.745 --> 12:44.379
Just drop and go.

12:44.380 --> 12:46.780
Uh, here, let me get
that check for you.

12:52.188 --> 12:53.388
Well, it's official.

12:53.389 --> 12:55.657
Nobody wants to bet against Chris now.

12:55.658 --> 12:56.992
Damn it! I can't believe my kid

12:56.993 --> 12:58.426
isn't making money for us anymore.

12:58.427 --> 13:00.862
I feel like Jessica Simpson's dad.

13:00.863 --> 13:02.897
Well, there are plenty
of guys willing to bet

13:02.898 --> 13:05.333
on James Woods High to
win, I'll tell you that.

13:05.334 --> 13:08.570
The only way we could ever make
money now is if Chris lost.

13:08.571 --> 13:10.730
Wait a minute, Joe, that's it!

13:10.731 --> 13:12.340
All we got to do is take those bets

13:12.341 --> 13:13.934
and get Chris to take a dive!

13:13.935 --> 13:15.074
Wait, hold on, Peter.

13:15.075 --> 13:18.013
You're gonna ask your own
son to lose on purpose?

13:18.014 --> 13:19.214
Damn, Quagmire!

13:19.215 --> 13:21.849
Your fridge gives you
water from the door?

13:25.254 --> 13:26.988
Hey, champ, what you doing?

13:26.989 --> 13:28.590
My Spanish homework.

13:28.591 --> 13:31.470
Oh, well, then maybe I'll just
say this to you in Spanish.

13:31.471 --> 13:32.400
_

13:32.401 --> 13:37.197
_

13:37.198 --> 13:41.479
_

13:41.784 --> 13:42.783
_

13:42.784 --> 13:47.619
_

13:47.620 --> 13:50.175
_

13:50.176 --> 13:51.489
_

13:58.142 --> 14:00.279
Chris, what the hell are you doing?!

14:00.280 --> 14:02.548
Calm down. This is how
they package Snapple now.

14:02.549 --> 14:04.383
They're trying to trick
kids into drinking it.

14:04.384 --> 14:05.818
You may not believe this,

14:05.819 --> 14:08.087
but there was a time when
Snapple ruled the nation.

14:08.088 --> 14:09.488
Preposterous!

14:09.489 --> 14:11.790
It's true. Even Jerry
Seinfeld drank it.

14:11.791 --> 14:13.893
And he was the president of the '90s.

14:13.894 --> 14:16.195
But why are you so down?

14:16.196 --> 14:19.632
Dad told me I have to lose the
championship game on purpose.

14:19.633 --> 14:20.733
He what?!

14:20.734 --> 14:23.102
Peter, get in here right now!

14:23.103 --> 14:25.604
Wow, someone's day-horny!

14:25.605 --> 14:26.772
Oh, hey, Chris.

14:26.773 --> 14:28.407
Did you tell Chris he had to lose

14:28.408 --> 14:29.742
the district championship?!

14:29.743 --> 14:31.943
Let me just get a
garbage bag. Hold on.

14:35.315 --> 14:37.283
Okay, now that I'm decent.

14:37.284 --> 14:39.685
Yes, I did tell Chris
to throw the game.

14:39.686 --> 14:41.387
But it's okay; it's for gambling.

14:41.388 --> 14:44.256
What?! You're betting on
Chris's baseball team?!

14:44.257 --> 14:46.525
Technically against
Chris's baseball team.

14:46.526 --> 14:47.793
Are you crazy?!

14:47.794 --> 14:49.295
Do I look crazy?!

14:49.296 --> 14:51.163
What do you think puts
the food on our table

14:51.164 --> 14:52.631
and the garbage bags on our backs?!

14:52.632 --> 14:54.333
Chris, your father's a jackass.

14:54.334 --> 14:55.734
When you get on that field,

14:55.735 --> 14:57.903
you try your very
best and play to win.

14:57.904 --> 14:59.505
You understand me?

14:59.506 --> 15:01.640
Yeah. Thanks, Mom.

15:01.641 --> 15:03.242
But, Lois, if Chris wins that game,

15:03.243 --> 15:05.874
I'll be out a ton of money and
I'll have to kiss a fella!

15:05.875 --> 15:07.504
I take all kinds of bets.

15:11.885 --> 15:13.686
Hey, Frank, we have to talk.

15:13.687 --> 15:16.255
You've got to stop giving
away all the food for free.

15:16.256 --> 15:18.324
Yeah, otherwise there's no way
we're gonna make a profit.

15:18.325 --> 15:20.359
Oh, we don't have to
worry about money.

15:20.360 --> 15:22.895
I might be doing a Duets
thing with that Lady Goo-Ga.

15:22.896 --> 15:24.296
Uh-huh, that's wrong.

15:24.297 --> 15:25.698
Anyway, the restaurant's
gonna go under

15:25.699 --> 15:27.066
if you keep giving away food.

15:27.067 --> 15:28.500
All right, all right.

15:28.501 --> 15:29.802
Thank you, Frank.

15:29.803 --> 15:31.836
I appreciate you trying it my way.

15:32.687 --> 15:34.187
Thank you.

15:34.188 --> 15:35.222
What was that?

15:35.223 --> 15:36.490
Oh, I get 40 bucks

15:36.491 --> 15:38.878
every time somebody says "my way."

15:38.879 --> 15:40.660
Nancy gets 60.

15:45.032 --> 15:46.700
What do you mean Chris
won't take a dive?!

15:46.701 --> 15:48.335
We already took a ton of bets!

15:48.336 --> 15:49.636
Look, I'm sorry, you guys,

15:49.637 --> 15:51.905
but my hot piece-of-ass
wife says no way.

15:51.906 --> 15:54.474
It's a weird time to brag
about your wife, Peter.

15:54.475 --> 15:56.343
I don't know, I've just
been so horny today.

15:56.344 --> 15:57.978
Oh, man, I don't need to know that!

15:57.979 --> 15:59.246
Well, pull it together, Peter,

15:59.247 --> 16:00.981
'cause we're about to
lose a lot of money!

16:00.982 --> 16:02.616
I know.

16:02.617 --> 16:04.351
We're screwed once
Chris takes the mound

16:04.352 --> 16:06.186
with that awesome arm of his.

16:06.187 --> 16:08.989
Wait, so what you're saying
is Chris isn't the problem,

16:08.990 --> 16:10.290
his arm is.

16:10.291 --> 16:11.591
I guess.

16:12.878 --> 16:15.195
Okay. We hear you, Peter.

16:15.196 --> 16:17.297
Loud and clear.

16:17.298 --> 16:19.766
Yeah, we'll fix this problem.

16:19.767 --> 16:21.401
You guys are creeping me out.

16:21.402 --> 16:23.303
All right, I'm gonna
exit while discreetly

16:23.304 --> 16:25.271
checking out the hot
chick by the door.

16:32.246 --> 16:33.880
You guys heard what I heard, right?

16:33.881 --> 16:36.216
Peter just asked us
to break Chris's arm.

16:36.217 --> 16:37.617
Well, he intimated.

16:37.618 --> 16:38.885
I don't know what that means,

16:38.886 --> 16:41.321
but let's go rough up a
teenager for beer money!

16:41.322 --> 16:43.389
Oh, I call biting!

16:49.397 --> 16:52.098
Okay, there's the baseball
team's locker room right there.

16:52.099 --> 16:54.367
Perfect! And we look like
regular high school students,

16:54.368 --> 16:56.335
so we'll fit right in.

16:58.205 --> 17:00.574
Joe, are you sure about these clothes?

17:00.575 --> 17:03.777
Trust me. I bought the absolute
latest issue of Archie comics,

17:03.778 --> 17:06.478
and this is what the kids are wearing.

17:07.548 --> 17:09.549
Oh, hey, fellow teens.

17:09.550 --> 17:12.385
Wait a minute, teenagers
don't have wheelchairs!

17:12.386 --> 17:15.354
No! Oh, no!

17:20.628 --> 17:23.229
Okay, guys, we've served
our last free meal.

17:23.230 --> 17:25.531
Here I go with the check.

17:26.567 --> 17:27.834
Oh, I'm sorry.

17:27.835 --> 17:29.169
Last time we ate here,

17:29.170 --> 17:31.538
Mr. Sinatra's son said it was free.

17:31.539 --> 17:33.239
Okay, uh, everyone, new policy!

17:33.240 --> 17:35.241
As is the case with many restaurants,

17:35.242 --> 17:37.644
you're going to have
to pay for your food.

17:37.645 --> 17:40.280
What? This food ain't
worth paying for.

17:40.281 --> 17:43.182
Yeah, the only reason we eat
here is 'cause it's free.

17:44.418 --> 17:46.886
Look whose restaurant
thinks it's so good!

17:46.887 --> 17:49.756
Oh, yeah? If it was Joey's
restaurant, you would've paid.

17:51.192 --> 17:52.993
Ma!

17:52.994 --> 17:54.327
I'm sorry, Ma!

17:54.328 --> 17:56.392
Ma!

17:57.102 --> 17:58.637
I can't believe it.

17:58.638 --> 17:59.839
They hated us.

17:59.840 --> 18:01.810
Well, fellas, we gave
it our best shot.

18:01.811 --> 18:03.770
If you need me, I'll be
back in Palm Springs,

18:03.771 --> 18:06.653
which has been completely
taken over by the gays.

18:07.608 --> 18:09.709
So, want to grab whatever wine is left

18:09.710 --> 18:11.111
and then burn the place down?

18:11.112 --> 18:13.113
Maybe, but first, let's
have an unearned

18:13.114 --> 18:15.248
end-of-the-series moment
where we turn out the lights

18:15.249 --> 18:16.715
on our own place.

18:18.986 --> 18:21.520
Sorry, pal, we're closed.

18:46.658 --> 18:48.492
Peter, we've got great news!

18:48.493 --> 18:49.826
Chris isn't playing!

18:49.827 --> 18:51.161
He's not? Why?

18:51.162 --> 18:53.274
Well, 'cause we broke his
arm like you told us to.

18:53.275 --> 18:54.943
Shattered. We shattered his arm.

18:54.944 --> 18:57.078
You what?! I never
told you to do that!

18:57.079 --> 18:59.114
You didn't? That's what
I thought I heard.

18:59.115 --> 19:02.117
Quagmire, this is humbling,
but it may be time

19:02.118 --> 19:04.619
for all of us to talk
about hearing aids.

19:04.620 --> 19:07.054
I feel terrible! I got
to go find my son!

19:10.440 --> 19:11.326
Chris!

19:11.327 --> 19:14.395
Dad, my arm's broke!
And look, a Camaro!

19:14.396 --> 19:16.564
Oh, that guy must be so boss.

19:16.565 --> 19:19.400
But listen, Chris, I had no
idea this was gonna happen.

19:19.401 --> 19:21.369
Look, I was wrong to
bet on your games,

19:21.370 --> 19:23.738
and it's even worse that
I told you to lose.

19:23.739 --> 19:25.006
I'm so sorry.

19:25.007 --> 19:26.374
Oh, that's okay, Dad.

19:26.375 --> 19:28.409
I just feel bad that my arm is broken

19:28.410 --> 19:31.312
in so many places and hurts so much.

19:31.313 --> 19:33.581
No, Chris, I've been a
terrible dad lately.

19:34.146 --> 19:35.784
You found something you were great at,

19:35.785 --> 19:37.585
and instead of being happy for you,

19:37.586 --> 19:39.687
I tried to use it to make money.

19:39.688 --> 19:43.158
And now your arm is broken and
your baseball career is over.

19:43.159 --> 19:44.759
Not necessarily.

19:44.760 --> 19:46.127
What? What are you talking about?

19:46.128 --> 19:48.329
Well, for the last few
weeks, since my right arm's

19:48.330 --> 19:52.300
been exhausted from pitching,
my left arm's had to, uh,

19:52.301 --> 19:55.164
pick up the slack in the bathroom.

20:08.304 --> 20:09.551
You see the pitcher?

20:09.552 --> 20:10.840
That's my kid.

20:15.057 --> 20:16.624
Aah! Son of a bitch!

20:16.625 --> 20:18.059
Oh, my God!

20:18.060 --> 20:19.727
Sorry, Mr. Quagmire!

20:19.728 --> 20:21.529
I heard that bone break.

20:21.530 --> 20:23.664
My ears are fine.

20:27.469 --> 20:29.737
Well, Chris, we're very proud of you

20:29.738 --> 20:31.673
for making it to the
district championship.

20:31.674 --> 20:33.141
Thanks, Mom.

20:33.142 --> 20:34.642
It was really something, Lois.

20:34.643 --> 20:37.145
The next pitch Chris threw
hit his coach in the head,

20:37.146 --> 20:39.647
so there was no one to
take him out of the game.

20:39.648 --> 20:41.583
Chris walked the next 46 batters.

20:41.584 --> 20:42.851
State record.

20:42.852 --> 20:45.119
Wow, Chris! State record!

20:45.120 --> 20:46.667
Yeah, they got crushed.

20:46.668 --> 20:48.256
But at least I didn't have to pay out

20:48.257 --> 20:49.924
all those bets and kiss a guy.

20:49.925 --> 20:52.789
But I saw you kissing the
driver of that Camaro.

20:52.790 --> 20:54.924
That... that-that was something else.

20:56.187 --> 20:57.522
Baseball!

20:57.523 --> 20:59.523
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru